  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe post sends Z, then X/Y, then the move with the rotary words (`fanuc.cps` `traverseZ`, `xyFirst`, `onRapid`). During the X/Y traverse, each rotary that turns the work stands where the previous program left it. The #2965 laws read one fitted axis or the part frame, so two cases were not judged (#3084).\n\n- New law `sim::verify::first_traverse_low_posed` (`crates/sim/src/verify/first_traverse_posed.rs`). It reads the start stock, the part and the tagged steel through every pose:\n  - two or more work-turning rotaries: on the sphere about the WCS origin;\n  - one work-turning rotary that tilts: a full turn about its line through the WCS origin.\n- New seam `operation::first_traverse_posed` (`crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse_posed.rs`). It reads:\n  - a rotary kind on a machine where two or more rotaries turn the work;\n  - a multi-axis kind on a machine where a tilting rotary turns the work.\n- A lone work-turning rotary with no usable axis line refuses generation by name.\n- The verdict is the blocking `FirstTraverseLow`. It replaces each first-traverse verdict at a lower top.\n- The op stamp of a newly judged operation takes the word `first-traverse-posed-3084`. No shipped project moves.\n- `first_traverse::judge` and the swept law do not change. `generate.rs` calls the new seam after each `judge` call.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3084-posed-first-traverse.md` (premises, limits, dropped options).\n\n## Readings\n\n- Two rotaries, rotary kind, laid square bar: the stock corner is 18.815 from the WCS origin. Clearance 12 is held (the fitted-axis law read 9.899). Clearance 20 passes.\n- Table A, 5-Axis Contour over the dome: the stock edge turns up to 23.324 about A. Clearance 20 is held (the part frame read 12). Clearance 25 passes.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/first_traverse_posed.rs`:\n  - `two_work_turning_rotaries_read_the_rotary_kinds_stock_on_its_sphere`\n  - `a_tilting_table_reads_a_5_axis_kinds_stock_swept_about_its_line`\n  - `a_work_turning_rotary_with_no_line_refuses_by_name`\n- `camcraft-sim` lib, `verify::first_traverse_posed::tests` (4 tests).\n\n## Gate (head 4664df470, local, debug)\n\n- `camcraft-sim` lib `first_traverse`: 12 passed.\n- `camcraft-app` tests: `first_traverse_posed` 3, `first_traverse_rotary` 3, `first_traverse_table` 9, `rotary_contour_x` 2, `microarc_test_part` 4, `index_swing` 13, `setup_align_multiaxis` 10, `continuous_4axis_part` 10, `first_4axis_part` 4, `example_catalog` 33 (2 ignored). All passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: not run, covered by the cut gate.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A program that starts low near the work (premise of PR #2997).\n- A 3+2 operation and a cross drill on a work-tilting machine: follow-up #3100. Refs #3100.\n- The two held tests check the post refusal with `is_err` only. They do not check its text, because the index-swing clause can refuse first.\n\nChangelog: The first-traverse check now reads the work through every pose of the machine's work-turning rotaries: a rotary kind on a machine with two such rotaries, and a multi-axis kind on a machine whose table tilts. A traverse under the turned-up work holds the post by name.\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #3084\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
